## Overview

This project was completed as part of a Forage Data Analytics Job Simulation.

The project involved analysing machine and factory data using Tableau to identify patterns in machine health and potential downtime. 
As well as which location the machines broke most often.

This was my first completed data analytics project and I used it to practise data preparation, calculated fields, data visualisation, dashboards, and drawing business insights from data.

## Tools Used

* Tableau
* Data visualisation
* Calculated fields
* Dashboard creation
* Data analysis

## Project Tasks

 1. Data Preparation

I imported the provided dataset into Tableau and explored the available fields, including factory location, device type, and machine status.

 2. Calculated Field — Unhealthy

I created a calculated field called `Unhealthy`.

The calculation assigned 10 minutes of potential downtime to each record where the machine status was `Unhealthy`. The formula I used was as below.

```text
IF LOWER(TRIM([Status])) = "unhealthy" THEN 10
ELSE 0
END
```

I used `LOWER()` and `TRIM()` to make the calculation more reliable when working with text data.

 3. Down Time per Factory

I created a bar chart showing potential downtime across factories in different locations.

This allowed me to compare factories and identify locations with higher levels of potential downtime.

4. Down Time per Device Type

I created a second bar chart comparing potential downtime by device type.

The analysis showed that:

* LaserWelder recorded 480 minutes of potential downtime.
* LaserCutter recorded 430 minutes of potential downtime.

LaserWelder therefore had the highest potential downtime among the device types observed in this analysis.

 5. Interactive Dashboard

I combined the two visualisations into an interactive Tableau dashboard.

The factory chart was configured as a filter so that selecting a factory updates the device-type chart to show the relevant machines for that factory.

## Key Insight

The analysis indicated that LaserWelder and LaserCutter had notably higher potential downtime than other device types. 
LaserWelder recorded 480 minutes (8 hours) of potential downtime, while LaserCutter recorded 430 minutes (7 hours 10 minutes).
The location that the machines break the most was Osaka, Japan. 

These device types may warrant closer monitoring or further investigation to understand the reasons behind their higher number of unhealthy records.

## What I Learned

Through this project, I practised:

* Importing and exploring data in Tableau
* Working with dimensions and measures
* Creating calculated fields
* Using conditional logic in Tableau
* Creating bar charts
* Building interactive dashboards
* Using one visualisation as a filter
* Interpreting data and identifying business insights
* Communicating findings using data visualisations

## Project Outcome

This project helped me develop practical experience with Tableau and gave me an opportunity to apply data analysis concepts to a realistic business scenario.

